    {
      "paragraph_id": "snow-country-zh-p00818",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "“人嘛，都是脆弱的。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "People are fragile, after all.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "snow-country-zh-p00818",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "据说从高处摔下来，就会粉身碎骨。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "They say that if you fall from a high place, your body will be smashed to pieces.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "snow-country-zh-p00818",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "可是，熊什么的，从更高的岩石山上摔下来，一点也不会受伤。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "But bears and the like can fall from even higher rocky mountains and not be hurt at all.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
